# Installed as /etc/sudoers.d/voice-proposals by scripts/install-local.sh.
#
# One direction only: the OWNER may run the proposals CLI as the restricted
# agent account. The owner-side broker and the owner's approving agent seat
# therefore read and write the proposal store through the agent's own binary
# and its own database, and no part of this feature hands the agent account a
# GitHub token, a new command, or any additional privilege - the rules that
# bound voice-agent live in /etc/sudoers.d/voice-agent and are untouched here.
#
# The command is pinned to the proposals subcommand with the system config:
# it can list, show and transition proposals, and it can do nothing else as
# voice-agent.
#
# The installer rewrites the user field below to whoever ran it; `pi` is the
# owner account on the reference device and keeps this file a complete,
# checkable sudoers file (`visudo -cf packaging/voice-proposals-sudoers`)
# rather than an unvalidatable template.
pi ALL=(voice-agent) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/voice --config /etc/voice/config.json proposals *
